KG42.register("clusters-de507c8d97e5bece7d5a1601",{"id":"37-dsm_auction_incentives::v142-d-CL001","paper":"37-dsm_auction_incentives","label":"Demand-information declaration, receipt, and historical retention","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Demand-information declaration, receipt, and historical retention","market_meaning":"Registered users submit the demand and related information for the next consumption period according to the method used; the distribution company receives the declarations and keeps historical declaration and electricity-use records, forming an information entry point that can be referenced for scheduling and billing.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The two chains belong to the information handover of the same DSM mechanism. Method 1 directly declares utility parameters, while Method 2 computes utility parameters from the consumption plan; the tuple definitions of the two methods are retained separately. Truthful declaration is a requirement, and this cannot be taken as establishing that the truthfulness incentive already holds.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The declaration content and the receipt and custody responsibilities form a candidate rule through an explicit information handover. The boundary stops at information formation and custody; configuration selection, billing and price updating each retain their own decision scope.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specifies the declaration obligation for the next period and the respective information content of the two methods."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplies the distribution company's receipt responsibility and historical-record custody obligation."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-C01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"],"rationale":"The declaration chain specifies the information submitted by users, and the coordination chain specifies that the same distribution company receives and keeps the relevant records; the smart-meter upload and the Table I submission step support this responsibility handover. This mapping does not create a record-processing algorithm or new scientific edges."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"Both places are the existing node of user demand submission in the same mechanism; the declaration-chain reference is selected for presentation, and both original references are fully retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The hat notation and utility-parameter notation in the Table I submission row have not yet been unified with the method definitions in the main text, and that row cannot be used directly to rewrite the declaration tuples of the two methods.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X002","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X003","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X004","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X005","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e011"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the hat notation, submission fields and method scope in the original table and main text, and have upstream record the differences explicitly; D retains the existing objects and does not merge the tuples of the two methods."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Method 2 only states that utility parameters are computed based on user type, appliance type and planned demand, and it lacks a reproducible computation rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g03-e05"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B is to determine the computation scheme and whether it is explicitly stated in the paper, and then C is to supplement the applicable conditions and object bindings; if the original text does not provide them, explicitly retain this computation gap."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Utility information, the consumption feasible region and the appliance plan are currently all carried by the generic demand-submission node. The related utility-parameter declaration proposal remains pending.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g03-e03","v141-b-g03-e04","v141-b-g03-e05"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p01","v141-b-g03-p02"],"required_work":"Manually check the scope carried by the existing node and handle the listed proposals; this assembly does not approve proposals or add nodes."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence supporting the declaration-and-custody handover all remains unverified; this experiment permits only the formation of candidates to be checked on that basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g03-e03","v141-b-g03-e04","v141-b-g03-e05"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequent manual work is to check the original pages, transcriptions and scope; retain the current source_status and do not describe candidate status as source or scientific conclusions having undergone independent verification."}]},"rule_refs":["37-dsm_auction_incentives::v141-c-R001","37-dsm_auction_incentives::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["KG40-14a3066c15f25075","KG40-3482a1190712c456"]});
